00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.000
Carmen Cruickshank: How are you guys?

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Alexis: Good.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Shannon Lee: All right.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:23.000
Carmen Cruickshank: That's good. Okay, my Fathom note taker is joining twice. I'm just going to…

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Carmen Cruickshank: See what's going on…

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Okay, just to check, does anyone have any schedule needs, or, like, they need to get first, or they're, like, on a time crunch, just…

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.000
Shannon Lee: Um, my…

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Shannon Lee: My dad just randomly called me and asked if I wanted to go to lunch, so I just had, like, one quick question that I wanted to ask, and then hop off, if that's okay.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yeah.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.000
Alexis: Yeah, totally fine.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:50.000
Alexis: Because I'm going to take a minute. So yeah, go ahead, Shannon.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:01:04.000
Shannon Lee: Okay, okay. I just, um, wanted to ask your thoughts on adding, like, wedding venue keywords. So, I'm a wedding photographer, and I didn't know if adding to my, like, Google Ads keywords, like…

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:51.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Okay. Yeah.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:17.000
Shannon Lee: Um, for example, Bella Cosa is a wedding venue that's near me that's really popular. Like, if I put in, like, Bella Cosa wedding photographer as one of my Google Ads words, is that a good idea? Is that a bad idea?

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:31.000
Carmen Cruickshank: I think that'd be a good idea, because I don't think it would deter too much from your actual… like, it's not too irrelevant, or it wouldn't be, like, so out there that it's, like, Google is confused. Um, I want to see how many keywords you have right now.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:37.000
Shannon Lee: I keep getting the warning that I, like, don't have enough relevant keywords, um…

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Real quick.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:41.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yeah, they'll do that sometimes. I think it's, like, good knowing, uh…

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:50.000
Carmen Cruickshank: the context, if… because some people actually are missing relevant keywords, and then it's like, okay, like, we'll add some of those. I don't know if we did that last time to your account, if we added some.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:51.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Ah.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:54.000
Shannon Lee: I think we decided that we were fine on my end.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:59.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Okay. Yeah, we just have one ad group with the — I probably should share my screen real quick.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.000
Shannon Lee: Um, with the keywords.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:01.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Let's see…

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:09.000
Carmen Cruickshank: So, one campaign…

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:12.000
Carmen Cruickshank: With the photographer.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:14.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Add, sir.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.000
Carmen Cruickshank: And then how many…

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:22.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Okay, so we have 18, maybe 17 keywords.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:33.000
Carmen Cruickshank: I think that that's pretty much a good amount. I think, if anything, we would actually have to cut out some keywords, not like we have to do that right now, but for example, the bottom…

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:40.000
Carmen Cruickshank: 9 are not really getting as many clicks, so as you can see, we only really have, like, top 4.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:46.000
Carmen Cruickshank: So I don't think we'd need to add more, but I think if you wanted to add, did you say it was Bella Rosa or Bella C.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:03:01.000
Shannon Lee: I mean, I can go in and add it too at some point. I just didn't know if it was a good idea or if I should use it to replace it. I'm not even set if that's the venue I'm going to use my keyword.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:03.000
Shannon Lee: time towards, I guess.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:02.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Okay.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:13.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yeah, I think you could definitely add it, and I don't think it would have any issue, because also, like, we're adding… it's not really random, but almost, like, random locations, St. Peter… St. Petersburg, Jupiter…

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:19.000
Carmen Cruickshank: And then it's just kind of telling Google what type of searches we want. So I think adding one or two wouldn't harm it at all.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:25.000
Shannon Lee: Okay. Do you think I should replace some of the low-performing ones with, like, new tests?

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:35.000
Carmen Cruickshank: I think if you just wanted to pause maybe the lowest 5 performing ones, just to kind of, like… you could just… do you know how to pause them, or…

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:36.000
Shannon Lee: Mm-hmm.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:42.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Okay, yeah, so you just pause those, and you can just add in, like, one or two keywords of what you'd want, and I think that'd be good.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:47.000
Carmen Cruickshank: I'm just going to check performance over the past two weeks.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:55.000
Carmen Cruickshank: So click-through rate is good, you're definitely getting a good amount of clicks. Cost per conversion is going down, I think…

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:59.000
Carmen Cruickshank: I don't remember what it was before, but I think it was higher than 78.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:13.000
Shannon Lee: Yeah, I think it's going down. I'm now in my second month of the ads, so I know they're still learning. My Meta ads are doing better, but that is okay. I'm more familiar with that side of things, so I have a better…

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:09.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yeah, no, 100%.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:11.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yep.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:30.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yeah, no, that makes sense. And I also always really expect Meta to do better because number one, you get results way quicker. Google, no one's just like scrolling on Google. So it's definitely like, I think it's a good add-on, but I think it shouldn't be like a fully dependent use of ads, if that makes sense. Like it's helpful, but not super helpful.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:15.000
Shannon Lee: situation. But.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Just that, you know.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:40.000
Shannon Lee: Okay, awesome. That was my… that was my main question. Thank you so much, Alexis, for letting me hop in.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:35.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yep.

